### **Odoo Implementation Cost Matrix**




| **Cost Type** | **Description** | **Hours/Cost** | **Example Use Case** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1. Implementation Costs (CAPEX)** |  |  |  |
| Basic Implementation | Standard Odoo features with minimal customization or data migration. | **50 hours** | Small service or product based company with CRM and invoicing needs. |
| Small Business Implementation | Full standard implementation including one complex app (Production, Inventory or Accounting) with studio (light customisation) and more sophisticated data migration. No development. | **100 hours** | Service , production or product trading business with basic accounting. |
| Full ERP Implementation | Complex data migration, developments, and more complex app standard implementation. | **200 hours** | Manufacturing company using MRP, inventory management, etc. with full accounting. |
| Large-Scale Implementation | Includes custom development, complex data migration, implementation of more complex application (production, accounting, inventory) | **250+ hours** | Logistics or industrial company needing a enhanced business flow. A large scale implementation requires a business analysis before we start. |
| Integration with another software | Development required to connect Odoo to another software, coordinate inbetween parties, test and fine tune. | **100 hours** | Any company willing to integrate its ERP with a industry specific software. An integration requires a technical and data analysis before we start |
| **2. License Costs, recurring costs (OPEX)** |  |  |  |
| Standard Licenses | Standard features, no customization or multicompany. This type of license includes all Odoo applications. | **€24.90/month per user**, 19.90€/month the first year. | Company using basic Odoo functionality. |
| Custom Licenses | Allows customization (Odoo Studio), multicompany, required for Odoo SH or on-premise hosting. | **€37.40/month per user**, 29.90€/ month the first year. it is important to know that **75% of Odoo licenses are custom licences.** As an Official Odoo Partner, we often take care of more demanding project raising this proportion to 90% of our clients. | Retail chain managing multiple stores and custom workflows. |
| **3. Hosting Costs, recurring costs (OPEX)** |  |  |  |
| Free Hosting | Provided with standard license, no custom development or advanced integrations. | **Free** | Company using only standard Odoo apps without custom features. |
| Odoo SH Hosting | Required for custom development and easier access to database, backups, and logs. | **€780/year**, it is important to know that **the majority of Odoo databases worldwide are hosted on Odoo SH.** As an Official Odoo Partner, we often take care of more demanding project raising this proportion to 75% of our clients. | Manufacturing company with tailored MRP and production planning. |
| **4. Support & Maintenance, recurring (OPEX)** |  |  |  |
| Corrective Maintenance | Ongoing support for troubleshooting and issue resolution. | **Variable (Based on contract)**, most of our clients require inbetween **2 to 10 hours** of support monthly | Company requiring continuous support for operational issues and improvement. |
| Evolutive Maintenance | System migration (e.g., every 2-3 years) for Odoo SH or on-premise installations. | **Free**/ **€5 hours /migration** OR may require additional costs based on the complexity of the developments. |  |

An Odoo project could potentially be a one time 50 hours of service attached to € 24.90/ month license for a basic project but chances are you might required more than that to cover your specif needs.  
  
Finally, at Agitech we offer a range of possibilities to help our clients get their project funded by Sate Financial Aid (for Belgium and France) supporting innovation and digital transformation.




### **Key Takeaways**



* **Quick ROI**: Odoo delivers immediate value by automating processes, reducing manual tasks, and improving efficiency.
* **Cost-Effective**: Odoo is often five times more affordable than other ERP systems like SAP or Microsoft Dynamics, making it a cost-effective choice for any size of company
* **Strategic Investment**: Even a 200-hour implementation, which includes customizations and data migration, remains affordable for a company with an annual revenue of €250,000 or more. This is a small price to pay for a solution that will run your entire business.



### **Ready to Explore Odoo?**



If you’re considering Odoo, it’s important to approach it as a strategic investment. Our team at Agitech is here to guide you through every step of the process, ensuring that you get the most out of your Odoo implementation. Whether you’re a small business or a larger enterprise, Odoo offers the flexibility and scalability to grow with you.
